msgstr ""

#: a7a1aacf466649f28710d2a468d9e961 fc2c056760a243b59f41dbbf18df1301
msgid "applies their craft"
msgstr ""

#: 7ae66dac5c8f41cf977aebc34e351167
msgid "information"
msgstr ""

#: 16f5c558a40745189540a1b0f41057f1
msgid "reference"
msgstr ""

#: 5a27ba57d48a49a381a2895880d24de3 eed2283995a84877a34aa5a4f59df884
msgid "informs cognition"
msgstr ""

#: 42c3ec02df6740b88483ee663c0e727f
msgid "understanding"
msgstr ""

#: 2055e3bbff7e4efcbe004e86d44254df
msgid "explanation"
msgstr ""

#: 673c4efeb51d4e8c95cfc4a5bcbfafab
msgid ""
"The Diátaxis map of documentation is a memorable and approachable idea. "
"But, a map is only reliable if it adequately describes a reality. "
"Diátaxis is underpinned by a systematic description and analysis of "
"generalised **user needs**."
msgstr ""

#: 136fdadb841348599cc9192f58ff1d66
msgid ""
"This is why the tutorials, how-to guides, reference and explanation of "
"Diátaxis are a complete enumeration of the types of documentation that "
"serve practitioners in a craft. This is why there are four and only four "
"types of documentation. There is simply no other territory to cover."
msgstr ""

